 "root_cause": "MediaProcessor configured stderr=PIPE without a consumer. A controlled stdlib child writing two bounded diagnostic bursts cannot reply on the old source until the test cleanup drains its pipe.",
 "changes": [
  "Continuously discard stderr in at most 4096-byte reads under an empty task/callback context",
  "Retain only saturating byte counts, logging one fixed event at normal EOF without diagnostic content",
  "Observe failed/cancelled readers before dispatch, reclaiming an old worker before replacement",
  "Ignore stale reader callbacks for later worker state",
  "Keep both process and diagnostic task references until actual reclamation and reader completion within one remaining cleanup budget"
 ],
